<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alhfrith</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 655–664</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alhfrith was a son of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oswiu">Oswiu of Northumbria</a> who ruled Deira as sub-king under his father from about 655. He married Cyneburh, a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penda-of-mercia">Penda of Mercia</a>, and supported the Roman party at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/synod-of-whitby">Synod of Whitby</a> in 664 as a patron of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilfrid">Wilfrid</a>. He disappears from the record soon afterwards, possibly after rebelling against his father.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alhfrith.jpg" alt="Alhfrith" width="320" height="423" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kmusser · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:British_7th_Century.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
